# Ship physics architecture (pointer)

Full law: [`docs/docs/architecture/ship-physics.md`](../../docs/docs/architecture/ship-physics.md).

**Permanent decision:** in vacuum, Newton holds — release thrust ≠ instant stop;
ship coasts. It does **not** coast forever: residual space drag + (when
**coupled**) thruster assist bleed velocity. **Decoupled** ≈ free coast.
**Pitch/yaw:** move mouse → **HUD cursor** moves → **ship turns toward that
cursor** (dual reticle: cursor instant, nose lags). Never snap attitude to
mouse. Same in atmosphere and vacuum. Atmosphere adds strong drag + planet *g*
([Ship flight](../../docs/docs/architecture/ship-flight.md)).
Rapier integrates; flight computer emits forces.

When changing vacuum coast, coupled bleed, residual drag, angular settle, or
mouse-cursor aim-track, read the full doc first. Also listed in `AGENTS.md`.
